 // The reach node is a child of the hand bone; AttackCollision::Update turns it world-aligned once a frame (Precision's
 // update runs at the start of the frame, before animation, so its tilt lags the hand by one frame's rotation).
 // Switches in Data/SKSE/Plugins/Precision_ZenderalFixes.ini, [UnarmedReach].
+//
+// Weapons (patch 0004, 2026-11-12): the blade does NOT reliably reach them either. A two-hander still missed rats
+// and spiders (player report 2026-11-12): the list's movesets swing at chest height, and Precision's spine pitch
+// toward the target (Collision_PitchMult) only tilts the swing. So a humanoid's melee weapon swing gets the same kind
+// of capsule, hanging straight down from up to four points along the blade (from fStartFraction of its length to the
+// tip, at most fSpacing apart), same rules: actors only, at most fMaxTargetHeightRatio x the attacker's height.
+// Each capsule is at least fMinLengthRatio x the attacker's height long, so a swing whose collision starts low still
+// reaches the ground when it rises. Switches in [WeaponReach].
 
 #include "ZenUnarmedReach.h"
 
